! vfl_cross_protect.strap -- address protection (DS) on VFL stores
! that cross a word boundary, and on CONNECT TO MEMORY's one-word store.
!
! THE RULES, Reference Manual 22-6530-2, read in the page images (PDF =
! printed + 3):
!   printed p.31, Definition of Monitored Area: the area is the word at
!   the lower boundary (location 3 bits 32-49) up to, not including, the
!   upper (bits 0-17); "When the boundary control bit is zero, a signal is
!   obtained for a comparand inside the specified area ... An instruction
!   or data field which straddles a boundary always gives an address
!   monitoring signal."
!   printed p.32: "When the interruption system is disabled, address
!   monitoring is ineffective"; "When an address alarm is caused by a
!   data address used in a store-type operation, indicator DS is turned
!   on.  Since this indicator is permanently masked on, storing in core
!   storage is always suppressed, and the operation is always terminated.
!   A store-type operation is one in which the contents of an addressed
!   storage location are subject to change."  Addresses Monitored, Data
!   Store: "1. The effective address of all store-type operations."
! So a crossing field whose SECOND word is protected is not stored, and
! a CM (store-type: it writes its field back) is monitored like ST.
!
! WHAT "TERMINATED" MEANS HERE: no store, none of the operation's result
! indicators (MOP, LC, PF, the result indicators) or connective counts --
! as ST's arm has done since 2026-10-24 -- AND NO PROGRESSIVE INDEX PART.
! printed p.22, Programming Notes: "If an exception condition is detected
! during the variable field length portion of the operation, the entire
! operation will be suppressed, and the appropriate indicator will be
! turned on.  However, if an exception condition is detected during the
! index modification portion of the operation, only this portion will be
! suppressed."  The protected store is in the VFL portion, so the index is
! neither advanced, counted nor refilled, and the index result indicators
! are not set (P4, P6; built 2026-11-17 -- before, ST, M+ and CM all ran
! their index part after DS).
!
! SET-UP, ds_terminates_branch.strap's shape: boundaries and the
! interruption address planted DISABLED; lower boundary PW1, upper PEND
! (so the area is PW1 alone), control bit 0 (signal inside); then BE.
! DS's interruption runs entry 19, "BB1, 6.0" -- word 6 bit 0 is the
! marker (in p.31's 0-31 carve-out, it cannot itself signal).  After each
! case eight NOPs give the interruption its boundary, TI copies the
! indicators and word 6, and BBZ clears the marker.  DS stays on "until
! [it causes] an interruption" (p.32), so the indicator words below show the operation's
! own settings only.
!
!   P1  M+(BU,8,8) acc 1, field FF at PW0+.60 (PW0 low nibble, PW1 top
!       nibble): PW1 is protected.  DS: PW0 = ..AF, PW1 = F5.. unchanged;
!       I1 = 0 (terminated); D1 = (16)8000000000000000.
!   P2  CONTROL: the same M+ at UW0+.60, outside the area: UW0 = ..A0,
!       UW1 = 05.., LC MOP RZ (16)20000000140 (= vfl_cross_tomemory's X1);
!       D2 = 0, no interruption.
!   P3  CM0101(BU,8,8) at PW1+.8, one word, protected: PW1 unchanged,
!       I3 = 0, D3 set.  (Stored with DS off until 2026-11-17.)
!   P4  CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at PW1+.24 through X7, count 1 (the refill
!       path): PW1 unchanged, I4 = 0, D4 set, and X7 NOT refilled: still
!       XPP, (16)01905800000405DD.
!   P5  CM0101(BU,16,8) at PW0+.56, crossing into PW1: unchanged, I5 = 0,
!       D5 set.
!   P6  ST(V+IC)(BU,8,8) at PW1+.40 through X6, count 5, no refill (the
!       shared trailing index block): PW1 unchanged, I6 = 0, D6 set, X6 NOT
!       counted: still XPQ, (16)01906800001405DD.
! CYCLES 1209 is a model pin.
! CYCLES 1209 -> 1196, 2026-11-17: the preparation floor (StretchCore's
! `ib` and rl_prepare's load clock; docs/atlas_oracle.md "Closing the
! residuals" item 7).  MEASURED with it removed: 1209 again; with the
! decode hold's old word set (storeWaitWord) instead: 1196, no effect.
! CYCLES 1196 -> 1225, 2026-11-20: interruption recovery (plan §1c 5f; Perf.
! Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-24) reruns the undone run-ahead; with the recovery
! window injected off, 1196 again.
!
! MEASURED INJECTIONS, 2026-11-17, on the final model (each in the
! worktree from a saved copy, restored and compared with cmp; observed on
! this deck and the other two new decks, vfl_cross_storewait and
! vfl_cross_special_words, which pass under all four; the rest of the
! suite was not run under them):
!   J2 vflFieldStore compares the first word only: FAIL P1_PW0 =
!      (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5BE, P1_PW1 = (16)EFA5A5A5A5A5A5A5 (P5's store),
!      I1 = (16)20000000140, D1 = 0, I5 = (16)120, D5 = 0, cycles = 1153.
!      P2, P3, P4, P6 pass.
!   J3 vflFieldStore compares a crossing field only (the old one-word CM):
!      FAIL P1_PW1 = (16)F501A501A5A5A5A5 (P3's and P4's bytes), I3 =
!      (16)120, D3 = 0, I4 = (16)9120, D4 = 0, X7_P4 =
!      (16)01348000013405DC (refilled), cycles = 1152.  I1, D1, P2, P5 and
!      P6 pass.
!   J4 the M+ arm sets its indicators over the suppressed store (the old
!      M+): FAIL I1 = (16)20000000140 ONLY.
!   J8 the index part runs after DS (StretchExecute.bsv as it was before
!      the p.22 change): FAIL I4 = (16)9000, X7_P4 = (16)01348000013405DC,
!      I6 = (16)1000, X6_P6 = (16)01906800001005DD, cycles = 1211.
! P2 is the control: it passes under every injection.
!
        SLC, 1000.0
START   BD,  $+.32
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, PW1
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := PW1
        LVI, $X13, PEND
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := PEND
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit 0: signal INSIDE
        LX,  $X7, XPP
        LX,  $X6, XPQ
        BE,  $+.32
! ---- P1: crossing M+, second word protected -----------------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), PW0+.60
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        TI, 1, 6, D1
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
! ---- P2: the control, the same M+ into unprotected words ---------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), UW0+.60
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        TI, 1, 6, D2
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
! ---- P3: one-word CM into a protected word ------------------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        CM0101(BU,8,8), PW1+.8
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        TI, 1, 6, D3
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
! ---- P4: one-word CM with a refill, into a protected word ---------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X7), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        TI, 1, 6, D4
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X7, X7A                ! X7 not advanced, not refilled
! ---- P5: crossing CM, second word protected -----------------------
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        Z, $IND
        CM0101(BU,16,8), PW0+.56
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I5
        TI, 1, 6, D5
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
! ---- P6: one-word progressive ST, no refill, protected word -------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        ST(V+IC)(BU,8,8), 0($X6), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I6
        TI, 1, 6, D6
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X6, X6A                ! X6 not advanced, not counted
        BD,  $+.32
PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, 1500.0
XPP     XW, PW1+.24, 1, RFW      ! count 1: the refill fires
RFW     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0
XPQ     XW, PW1+.40, 5, RFW      ! count 5: no refill
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0100000000000000
HBEEF   DD(BU,64), (16)BEEF000000000000
UW0     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5

        SLC, 1600.0
PW0     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
PW1     DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
PEND    DD(BU,64), 0

        SLC, 1700.0
I1      DD(BU,64), 0
I2      DD(BU,64), 0
I3      DD(BU,64), 0
I4      DD(BU,64), 0
I5      DD(BU,64), 0
D1      DD(BU,64), 0
D2      DD(BU,64), 0
D3      DD(BU,64), 0
D4      DD(BU,64), 0
D5      DD(BU,64), 0
I6      DD(BU,64), 0
D6      DD(BU,64), 0
X7A     DD(BU,64), 0
X6A     DD(BU,64), 0

        SLC, 1800.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, 1819.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
